FIGURE's patch 1 of 2 to ImGuiColorTextEdit (goossens fork, commit 9f812a0 (2026-11-13)).

TextEditor::compressMarkers, run after any deletion while markers exist, stores each kept marker's new index in a
`bool`: every index above 1 becomes 1, so a third marker and the ones after it point at the second one's colour and
tooltip once a character is deleted anywhere. The index is a size_t. (compressSquiggles has the same field; FIGURE does
not use squiggles and leaves it.) Applied to third_party/ImGuiColorTextEdit/TextEditor.cpp; checked by
src/tests/figure_test_editor.F90 (marks kept on their lines after an edit). To report upstream.

--- a/TextEditor.cpp
+++ b/TextEditor.cpp
@@ -2238,7 +2238,7 @@
 		// references to current markers
 		struct Reference {
 			bool used = false;
-			bool index = 0;
+			size_t index = 0;
 		};
 
 		std::vector<Reference> references(markers.size());
